  "domain": "standards",
  "definition": "The Khronos Group is an open, member-driven industry consortium founded in January 2000 that creates and maintains royalty-free open standards for graphics, parallel compute, media, and extended reality APIs across heterogeneous hardware platforms. Its portfolio spans OpenGL, Vulkan, OpenCL, OpenXR, glTF, NNEF, WebGL, and SPIR-V, forming the portable API foundation that underpins GPU-accelerated rendering, XR runtimes, and cross-vendor compute across the technology industry. Khronos operates through working groups composed of member companies \u2014 including NVIDIA, AMD, Intel, ARM, Apple, Google, and Meta \u2014 that collaboratively draft, ratify, and publish specifications under open licences with conformance test suites.",
